WEBVTT

00:04.030 --> 00:16.866
Your Excellencies, UN Secretary General, President of the General Assembly, Executive Director of UN Women, and distinguished guests.

00:19.369 --> 00:23.274
Today, we are launching a campaign called HeForShe.

00:25.156 --> 00:29.562
I am reaching out to you because we need your help.

00:29.582 --> 00:33.987
We want to end gender inequality, and to do this,

00:34.827 --> 00:38.472
We need everyone involved.

00:38.492 --> 00:40.855
This is the first campaign of its kind at the UN.

00:41.876 --> 00:48.965
We want to try and galvanize as many men and boys as possible to be advocates for change.

00:48.985 --> 00:51.548
And we don't just want to talk about it.

00:51.568 --> 00:53.691
We want to try and make sure that it's tangible.

00:56.394 --> 01:01.600
I was appointed as Goodwill Ambassador for UN Women six months ago.

01:01.620 --> 01:03.703
And the more I've spoken about feminism,

01:04.358 --> 01:15.094
the more I have realized that fighting for women's rights has too often become synonymous with man-hating.

01:15.114 --> 01:24.428
If there is one thing I know for certain, it is that this has to stop.

01:24.448 --> 01:27.953
For the record, feminism by definition

01:28.945 --> 01:34.335
is the belief that men and women should have equal rights and opportunities.

01:35.657 --> 01:44.994
It is the theory of the political, economic, and social equality of the sexes.

01:45.014 --> 01:48.220
I started questioning gender-based assumptions a long time ago.

01:49.178 --> 01:58.689
When I was eight, I was confused at being called bossy because I wanted to direct the plays that we would put on for our parents.

01:59.871 --> 02:00.792
But the boys were not.

02:02.614 --> 02:06.999
When at 14, I started to be sexualized by certain elements of the media.

02:08.561 --> 02:15.810
When at 15, my girlfriends started dropping out of their beloved sports teams because they didn't want to appear muscly.

02:17.275 --> 02:24.626
when at 18, my male friends were unable to express their feelings.

02:24.646 --> 02:31.477
I decided that I was a feminist, and this seemed uncomplicated to me.

02:31.497 --> 02:40.511
But my recent research has shown me that feminism has become an unpopular word.

02:40.531 --> 02:45.679
Women are choosing not to identify as feminist.

02:48.224 --> 03:08.127
Apparently, I am among the ranks of women whose expressions are seen as too strong, too aggressive, isolating, and anti-men, unattractive even.

03:08.147 --> 03:12.632
Why has the word become such an uncomfortable one?

03:15.656 --> 03:16.577
I am from Britain.

03:17.924 --> 03:22.270
And I think it is right that I am paid the same as my male counterparts.

03:24.012 --> 03:28.719
I think it is right that I should be able to make decisions about my own body.

03:30.421 --> 03:42.598
I think... I think it is right

03:42.713 --> 03:48.781
that women be involved on my behalf in the policies and the decisions that will affect my life.

03:50.684 --> 03:56.732
I think it is right that socially I am afforded the same respect as men.

03:59.415 --> 04:10.290
But sadly, I can say that there is no one country in the world where all women can expect to receive these rights.

04:11.688 --> 04:19.699
No country in the world can yet say that they have achieved gender equality.

04:19.719 --> 04:27.269
These rights I consider to be human rights, but I am one of the lucky ones.

04:27.290 --> 04:34.459
My life is a sheer privilege because my parents didn't love me less because I was born a daughter.

04:35.921 --> 04:40.007
My school did nccot limit me because I was a girl.

04:41.557 --> 04:50.310
My mentors didn't assume that I would go less far because I might give birth to a child one day.

04:50.330 --> 04:57.461
These influences were the gender equality ambassadors that made me who I am today.

04:57.481 --> 05:03.009
They may not know it, but they are the inadvertent feminists who are changing the world today.

05:04.652 --> 05:05.774
We need more of those.

05:07.016 --> 05:08.678
And if you still hate the word,

05:09.772 --> 05:13.056
It is not the word that is important.

05:14.357 --> 05:18.842
It's the idea and the ambition behind it.

05:18.862 --> 05:23.107
Because not all women have received the same rights that I have.

05:24.368 --> 05:29.094
In fact, statistically, very few have been.

05:31.576 --> 05:37.483
In 1997, Hillary Clinton made a famous speech in Beijing about women's rights.

05:38.375 --> 05:43.603
Sadly, many of the things that she wanted to change are still true today.

05:45.726 --> 05:53.698
But what stood out for me the most was that less than 30% of the audience were male.

05:56.082 --> 06:07.118
How can we affect change in the world when only half of it is invited or feel welcome to participate in the conversation?

06:07.138 --> 06:07.639
Men.

06:09.914 --> 06:15.500
I would like to take this opportunity to extend your formal invitation.

06:17.302 --> 06:34.740
Gender equality is your issue too, because to date,

06:36.020 --> 06:45.392
I've seen my father's role as a parent being valued less by society, despite my needing his presence as a child as much as my mother's.

06:46.734 --> 06:58.028
I've seen young men suffering from mental illness, unable to ask for help, for fear it would make them less of a man.

06:59.662 --> 07:14.416
In fact, in the UK, suicide is the biggest killer of men, between 20 to 49, eclipsing road accidents, cancer, and coronary heart disease.

07:14.436 --> 07:22.363
I've seen men made fragile and insecure by a distorted sense of what constitutes male success.

07:24.204 --> 07:28.048
Men don't have the benefits of equality either.

07:29.902 --> 07:43.761
We don't often talk about men being imprisoned by gender stereotypes, but I can see that they are, and that when they are free, things will change for women as a natural consequence.

07:45.924 --> 07:53.314
If men don't have to be aggressive in order to be accepted, women won't feel compelled to be submissive.

07:54.756 --> 07:59.082
If men don't have to control, women won't have to be controlled

08:00.682 --> 08:03.789
Both men and women should feel free to be sensitive.

08:04.671 --> 08:07.938
Both men and women should feel free to be strong.

08:09.441 --> 08:16.817
It is time that we all perceive gender on a spectrum instead of two sets of opposing ideals.

08:25.403 --> 08:35.436
If we stop defining each other by what we are not and start defining ourselves by who we are, we can all be freer.

08:35.456 --> 08:37.979
And this is what HeForShe is about.

08:39.902 --> 08:42.966
It's about freedom.

08:42.986 --> 08:55.242
I want men to take up this mantle so that their daughters, sisters, and mothers can be free from prejudice, but also so that their sons have permission to be vulnerable and human too.

08:56.167 --> 09:06.780
We claim those parts of themselves they abandoned, and in doing so, be a more true and complete version of themselves.

09:06.800 --> 09:09.723
You might be thinking, who is this Harry Potter girl?

09:10.884 --> 09:13.848
And what is she doing speaking at the UN?

09:14.228 --> 09:16.051
And it's a really good question.

09:16.071 --> 09:18.073
I've been asking myself the same thing.

09:19.792 --> 09:25.241
All I know is that I care about this problem and I want to make it better.

09:26.523 --> 09:34.735
And having seen what I've seen and given the chance, I feel it is my responsibility to say something.

09:37.039 --> 09:47.335
Statesman Edmund Burke said, all that is needed for the forces of evil to triumph is for good men and women to do nothing.

09:50.099 --> 10:01.914
In my nervousness for this speech and in my moments of doubt, I've told myself firmly, if not me, who?

10:03.716 --> 10:05.718
If not now, when?

10:07.741 --> 10:18.334
If you have similar doubts when opportunities are presented to you, I hope that those words will be helpful because

10:20.018 --> 10:38.364
The reality is that if we do nothing, it will take 75 years, or for me to be nearly 100, before women can expect to be paid the same as men for the same work.

10:38.384 --> 10:44.372
15.5 million girls will be married in the next 16 years as children.

10:45.618 --> 10:58.755
And at current rates, it won't be until 2086 before all rural African girls can have a secondary education.

10:58.775 --> 11:07.266
If you believe in equality, you might be one of those inadvertent feminists that I spoke of earlier.

11:07.286 --> 11:11.151
And for this, I applaud you.

11:11.171 --> 11:14.595
We are struggling for a uniting word

11:14.879 --> 11:18.784
But the good news is that we have a uniting movement.

11:20.405 --> 11:21.787
It is called HeForShe.

11:24.210 --> 11:34.642
I am inviting you to step forward, to be seen, and to ask yourself, if not me, who?

11:36.384 --> 11:38.586
If not now, when?

11:40.509 --> 11:41.730
Thank you very, very much.

